score.role_fit.user_template:
Lead: {first_name} {last_name}
Role title: {role_title}
Company: {company_name}
Seniority signal: {seniority}

Scoring rubric:
- 1.0: Founder, CEO, CTO, VP Engineering, VP Product, Head of AI/ML, Head of Data
- 0.8: Co-founder (non-CEO), Director of Engineering at sub-50-person company, Principal PM at sub-100-person company
- 0.6: Senior Engineering Manager at sub-50-person company, Senior PM at sub-100-person company
- 0.4: IC engineer at sub-20-person startup (potential influencer), Director-level at 200+ person company (too far from decision)
- 0.2: IC at large company, mid-level non-technical roles
- 0.0: Sales, ops, HR, finance, intern, student

Return JSON with score (0.0-1.0) and one-sentence reasoning.

score.pain_signal.user_template:
Company: {company_name}
Industry: {industry}
Size: {employee_count}
Funding stage: {funding_stage}
Recent signals observed:
{signals_json}

Scoring rubric:
- 0.9-1.0: Hiring Head of AI/ML in last 90 days; founder posted publicly about AI strategy struggles; recently launched AI feature with mixed reception in press
- 0.7-0.8: Multiple AI/ML IC job posts active; recent funding round mentioning AI as use of proceeds; CEO/CTO posted thoughtful AI content on LinkedIn in last 30 days
- 0.4-0.6: One AI/ML job post; vague AI mentions in company materials; industry peers actively hiring AI
- 0.2-0.3: No active AI signals but technical company in a domain where AI adoption is expected
- 0.0-0.1: No relevant signals; company appears AI-mature with large internal team (we'd be redundant); company is in a domain where AI consulting fit is weak

Return JSON with score, one-sentence reasoning, and the single strongest signal observed (or 'none').

